WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
A couple of days after birth, nearly every

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.520
baby born in NSW is offered a heel-prick

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.120
blood test, checking for more than twenty conditions.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.480
One of them, PKU, can cause severe brain

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.280
damage, yet babies found this way can grow

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.560
up without it.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.360
So did the test prevent a genetic disease,

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.880
or only find it?

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.240
That's today's question: when can genetics help prevent

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.040
disease?

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:29.226
Genetic technologies do three different jobs.

00:00:29.547 --> 00:00:32.346
Screening finds a risk or a condition, but

00:00:32.427 --> 00:00:34.266
it doesn't change any DNA.

00:00:34.987 --> 00:00:38.986
Embryo testing chooses between embryos that already exist.

00:00:39.307 --> 00:00:43.066
Genetic engineering changes the genetic material itself.

00:00:43.707 --> 00:00:46.186
So for any method, ask which job it

00:00:46.347 --> 00:00:49.386
does, and what exactly it prevents: symptoms in

00:00:49.427 --> 00:00:52.106
a person, the birth of an affected child,

00:00:52.187 --> 00:00:54.186
or the faulty gene itself.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.040
Start with the heel prick.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.720
In PKU, short for phenylketonuria, both copies of

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.360
one gene are faulty, so the liver makes

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:07.880
too little working enzyme to break down phenylalanine,

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.040
an amino acid in ordinary protein.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.400
Phenylalanine builds up in the blood and damages

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:15.080
the developing brain.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.320
If the test finds it early, the baby

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.240
starts a low-phenylalanine diet straightaway, the level stays

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.480
low, and the brain develops normally.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.260
The faulty alleles are still there in every

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:30.140
cell, and they can still be passed on.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.420
What the diet prevents is the harmful phenotype,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.660
the effect the genes have on the body,

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.460
because it limits the phenylalanine the weak pathway

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:39.980
can't handle.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.540
That's why screening only helps when there's something

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.300
useful to do next.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.460
A test for a condition nothing can treat

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.860
finds it, but it doesn't prevent it.

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:52.786
The second job is finding risk before a

00:01:52.867 --> 00:01:53.506
pregnancy.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:57.106
You've met carriers before: people with one altered

00:01:57.307 --> 00:02:00.546
allele for a recessive condition like cystic fibrosis,

00:02:00.627 --> 00:02:03.826
plus one working copy, so they're usually healthy.

00:02:04.307 --> 00:02:05.426
Most don't know it.

00:02:06.147 --> 00:02:09.106
If two carriers have children, each pregnancy has

00:02:09.187 --> 00:02:11.106
a one in four chance of an affected

00:02:11.187 --> 00:02:11.746
child.

00:02:12.387 --> 00:02:15.186
Carrier screening tests a couple before or early

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.906
in pregnancy, and Medicare now funds it for

00:02:18.027 --> 00:02:20.946
three conditions, including cystic fibrosis.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:25.526
A genetic counsellor explains the options without steering

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.206
the couple's choice.

00:02:27.287 --> 00:02:31.286
One option is embryo testing, called PGT.

00:02:31.327 --> 00:02:34.006
The couple goes through IVF, and each embryo

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.326
grows for about five days.

00:02:36.407 --> 00:02:38.166
A few cells are taken from the outer

00:02:38.247 --> 00:02:40.966
layer, the part that would become placenta, and

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:43.606
tested for the family's known variant.

00:02:43.687 --> 00:02:46.886
Only an unaffected embryo is transferred.

00:02:46.967 --> 00:02:50.086
Notice that no embryo's DNA is changed.

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:53.526
PGT is selection, not engineering.

00:02:53.607 --> 00:02:56.246
It can prevent an affected birth, but only

00:02:56.327 --> 00:02:59.206
when the family's variant is already known, and

00:02:59.287 --> 00:03:01.606
it needs IVF, which is costly.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:05.513
The third job is changing genes.

00:03:05.794 --> 00:03:07.793
A change in a body cell stays with

00:03:07.874 --> 00:03:08.513
that person.

00:03:08.994 --> 00:03:11.153
Gene therapy works in body cells.

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:15.153
For spinal muscular atrophy, a modified virus carries

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.473
a working copy of a missing gene into

00:03:17.554 --> 00:03:19.633
nerve cells, and it has to be given

00:03:19.714 --> 00:03:22.833
early, before many of those cells are lost.

00:03:22.914 --> 00:03:25.393
For sickle cell disease, CRISPR can edit a

00:03:25.474 --> 00:03:28.833
patient's own blood stem cells outside the body.

00:03:28.994 --> 00:03:30.673
Both treat one person.

00:03:30.754 --> 00:03:32.753
Their children's risk doesn't change.

00:03:33.967 --> 00:03:37.326
Editing an egg, sperm or early embryo is

00:03:37.407 --> 00:03:39.326
called germline editing.

00:03:39.647 --> 00:03:42.366
The edit can enter the child's germline, their

00:03:42.447 --> 00:03:45.406
own eggs or sperm, and be inherited.

00:03:45.527 --> 00:03:48.286
That's the real difference from gene therapy: a

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:51.166
germline edit could be passed to children.

00:03:51.207 --> 00:03:53.059
It's illegal in Australia.

00:03:53.114 --> 00:03:55.886
The future person can't consent, a wrong edit

00:03:55.967 --> 00:03:58.286
could be inherited too, and it can't be

00:03:58.447 --> 00:03:59.166
taken back.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:03.606
So why can't genetics prevent most disease?

00:04:03.887 --> 00:04:06.086
The biggest limit is biology.

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:09.726
Type 2 diabetes, heart disease and most cancers

00:04:09.807 --> 00:04:13.326
involve many genes, each adding a little risk,

00:04:13.487 --> 00:04:15.966
plus diet and other exposures.

00:04:16.047 --> 00:04:18.286
There's no single gene to test for or

00:04:18.447 --> 00:04:21.606
edit, so prevention campaigns still do most of

00:04:21.647 --> 00:04:22.206
the work.

00:04:22.847 --> 00:04:25.566
Tests can also return a variant of uncertain

00:04:25.647 --> 00:04:28.686
significance, a DNA change no one can yet

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.606
call harmful or harmless.

00:04:31.247 --> 00:04:34.206
And methods that cost thousands or millions reach

00:04:34.287 --> 00:04:35.806
only some families.

00:04:37.034 --> 00:04:38.793
There are ethical questions too.

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.913
Couples have the right to make informed choices

00:04:42.034 --> 00:04:43.633
about their own families.

00:04:43.914 --> 00:04:46.953
But some disability advocates, including people who live

00:04:47.034 --> 00:04:49.913
with the conditions being tested for, argue that

00:04:49.994 --> 00:04:52.873
selecting against a condition sends a message about

00:04:52.954 --> 00:04:54.393
lives like theirs.

00:04:54.714 --> 00:04:56.833
And people disagree about where to draw the

00:04:56.874 --> 00:05:00.713
line, between a fatal childhood disease, an adult-onset

00:05:00.794 --> 00:05:02.153
one and a trait.

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:05.046
Two exam questions.

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:06.086
First.

00:05:06.407 --> 00:05:08.726
Carrier screening shows that both members of a

00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:12.326
couple carry a variant for spinal muscular atrophy,

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:14.886
an autosomal recessive condition.

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:18.086
State the chance that each pregnancy is affected.

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:21.366
Then explain how PGT could reduce the chance

00:05:21.407 --> 00:05:23.846
of an affected child, and why it isn't

00:05:23.927 --> 00:05:25.606
genetic engineering.

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:26.966
Pause here to answer.

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:38.246
One in four,

00:05:38.807 --> 00:05:41.286
because each carrier passes on the variant half

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:42.166
the time.

00:05:42.487 --> 00:05:46.006
With PGT, the couple's IVF embryos are tested

00:05:46.087 --> 00:05:48.886
for that known variant, and only an unaffected

00:05:48.967 --> 00:05:50.806
embryo is transferred.

00:05:50.927 --> 00:05:54.006
No DNA is altered, so it's selection, not

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:55.366
engineering.

00:05:55.447 --> 00:05:58.486
The classic mistake is writing that PGT removes

00:05:58.567 --> 00:06:00.246
the faulty gene from the embryo.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:01.946
Second.

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:06.106
Huntington's disease is caused by one dominant allele,

00:06:06.187 --> 00:06:08.666
and symptoms usually begin in adulthood.

00:06:08.987 --> 00:06:11.106
No current treatment prevents them.

00:06:11.467 --> 00:06:14.826
Explain why newborn screening would not prevent Huntington's

00:06:14.867 --> 00:06:15.466
disease.

00:06:16.107 --> 00:06:19.386
Then assess one genetic technology that could reduce

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:21.066
its effect on a family.

00:06:21.387 --> 00:06:22.746
Pause here to answer.

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:36.126
Screening only prevents symptoms when an early treatment

00:06:36.207 --> 00:06:38.966
exists, like the diet for PKU.

00:06:39.247 --> 00:06:42.526
Huntington's has none, so finding it early prevents

00:06:42.607 --> 00:06:43.086
nothing.

00:06:43.727 --> 00:06:47.086
PGT can select embryos without the known allele,

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:48.606
preventing an affected birth.

00:06:49.087 --> 00:06:51.646
But it needs IVF, costs a lot and

00:06:51.847 --> 00:06:55.006
raises ethical questions, so it helps some families,

00:06:55.087 --> 00:06:55.806
not most.

00:06:56.447 --> 00:06:59.166
The classic mistake is claiming gene therapy can

00:06:59.247 --> 00:07:00.206
now cure it.

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:04.633
So for any genetic prevention question, name the

00:07:04.794 --> 00:07:07.673
job: find, choose or change.

00:07:07.914 --> 00:07:11.753
Then say exactly what's prevented, symptoms, an affected

00:07:11.834 --> 00:07:14.553
birth or the gene itself, and give one

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:17.713
limit from biology, access or ethics.

00:07:17.994 --> 00:07:21.673
Next, a disorder that's already present: how technology

00:07:21.754 --> 00:07:23.193
can assist hearing loss.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:25.840
Here are the key notes.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.000
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:28.880
to copy them.
